        <detaileddescription>
<para>Isomorphism of vertices based on incident edges.</para><para>Given two pairs of vertices, (<computeroutput>i1</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>i2</computeroutput>) and (<computeroutput>j1</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>j2</computeroutput>), one from each of two graphs <computeroutput>g1</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>g2</computeroutput>, and given the two sets of edges that connect the vertices of each pair (in both directions), determine whether vertices <computeroutput>i2</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>j2</computeroutput> are isomorphic. The pair (<computeroutput>i1</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>j1</computeroutput>) is already part of a common subgraph isomorphism solution. Vertices <computeroutput>i2</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>j2</computeroutput> are already known to satisfy the <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Algorithm_1_1CsiEquivalence_1ab8f954ded387a67b3f434c4c9e513608" kindref="member">mu</ref> predicate and have the appropriate number of edges for inclusion into the solution.</para><para>This default implementation always returns true. </para>        </detaileddescription>
